Z||000000||Formula88||12-04-2001||04:17 PM||||Ok, so I'm looking to buy a digital camera sometime in the next month or so.  I'm not looking for the Uber-cam, but want something decent to take snapshots with.  I needs to be at least 1.3MPixel and I'm looking to spend around $200 (give or take).  <P>Any suggestions?  I've seen some from Kodak and Olympus that might fit the bill.  I like Sony, but don't know if they have anything in my price range.||||reg||5
Z||000001||JSocha||12-04-2001||04:21 PM||||Definately stay away from the Olympus 3030.  Its the biggest piece of junk we've ever had the displeasure of purchasing...twice!<P>Other then that, I hate digitals.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>EDIT: <BR>BTW, I have a SONY Mavica 7 something w/3.5" floppy drive.  Bought it back in '97 when Digital's were the rage.  $700.00 bucks down the drain...never use it...pictures suck no matter what you try...ended up buying a NIKON film camera, use it way more then I would a digital and get better pictures.  We bought a NIKON KOOLPIX 950 camera for the company.  They ask me to bring in my NIKON Film to take any pictures that they need.  Digital just never cuts it.<P>Just my $0.02. [/end of rant]<BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by JSocha (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||AusFiero||12-04-2001||04:28 PM||||I have a Kodak DC4800. Paid a mint for it  but have seen them on ebay for a little more than $200. They are 3.1 megapixel so it may be worth saving the extra bucks for and go ebaying.<P>By the way JSocha, digitals do cut it now but you do need the 3.1 megapixel ones. I just take my memory stick down to the local photolab and can get prints the same any camera. But personally I usually print them myself on photopaper using a HP 930C colour printer. The latter method is still not as "waterproof" as a development outlet. I also had a mavika, not much good for anything except web stuff.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero3.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A><p>[This message has been edited by AusFiero (edited 12-04-2001).]||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||12-04-2001||04:31 PM||||We bought a kodac DC215 millenium camera about 2 years ago..works great..<P>If you can, you should get a card reader with it (saves hassles when  transferring to your pc)<P>recommended specs<P>at least 1.3 mega pixel<BR>at least a 4-8 meg card<BR>automatic digital zoom (at least 2x)<P>Shop around & good luck!<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-04-2001||04:31 PM||||Thanks!  Yeah, I am a 35mm SLR man all the way - I just want digital capability for when it's convenient.  So, I'm not looking for a replacement for film, just something mainly for taking pics to email, etc.  But I still want decent picture quality if I want to, say, make desktop wallpapers of my Fiero, etc.||||reg||1
