Z||000006||Formula88||12-04-2001||04:46 PM||||Right now the ones I'm looking at are:<P>Kodak DX3500   2.2MPixel  $219.99<BR>Sony CyberShot DSC-P20   1.3MP   $199.95<BR>Olympus D-360L  1.3MP   $169.00  (serial connection, though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">)<P>And still looking....||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||12-04-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>Since you already got a 35mm SLR, and if you don't already as I don't know if you do, why not get a real good flat bed scanner?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Price.  Sure, the scanner isn't too expensive, but that adds the time and expense of developing film and scanning the pic.  That's too much trouble and expense for just snapshots.  With the digital camera, I can shoot endlessly and not worry about film, etc. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||JSocha||12-04-2001||05:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Price. Sure, the scanner isn't too expensive, but that adds the time and expense of developing film and scanning the pic. That's too much trouble and expense for just snapshots. With the digital camera, I can shoot endlessly and not worry about film, etc.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>Believe this or not, that was my entire "Sales Pitch" to myself.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I do have to admit, I was definately a good salesman, but a dumb customer for listening.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> hehehe  <P>Probably could have sold myself a glass a water if I was drowning too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
